    "readout_answer": "18",
    "readout_text": "To determine the number of digits in the base-ten representation of the expression:\n\n$$\n8^5 \\cdot 5^{10} \\cdot 15^5\n$$\n\nwe begin by simplifying the expression using prime factorization.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Prime Factorization\n\n- $8 = 2^3 \\Rightarrow 8^5 = (2^3)^5 = 2^{15}$\n- $5^{10}$ remains as is\n- $15 = 3 \\cdot 5 \\Rightarrow 15^5 = (3 \\cdot 5)^5 = 3^5 \\cdot 5^5$\n\nNow, combining all terms:\n\n$$\n8^5 \\cdot 5^{10} \\cdot 15^5 = 2^{15} \\cdot 5^{10} \\cdot 3^5 \\cdot 5^5 = 2^{15} \\cdot 3^5 \\cdot 5^{15}\n$$\n\nGroup the powers of 2 and 5:\n\n$$\n(2 \\cdot 5)^{15} \\cdot 3^5 = 10^{15} \\cdot 3^5\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Compute the Value\n\nWe now compute:\n\n$$\n10^{15} \\cdot 3^5\n$$\n\nWe know:\n\n- $3^5 = 243$\n- $10^{15}$ is a 1 followed by 15 zeros\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n10^{15} \\cdot 243 = 243 \\cdot 10^{15}\n$$\n\nThis is the number **243 followed by 15 zeros**, which is a 18-digit number.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Confirm Using Logarithms\n\nTo double-check, we can use the logarithmic method:\n\n$$\n\\log_{10}(10^{15} \\cdot 3^5) = \\log_{10}(10^{15}) + \\log_{10}(3^5) = 15 + 5 \\log_{10}(3)\n$$\n\nUsing the approximation $\\log_{10}(3) \\approx 0.4771$:\n\n$$\n5 \\log_{10}(3) \\approx 5 \\cdot 0.4771 = 2.3855\n$$\n\n$$\n\\log_{10}(N) \\approx 15 + 2.3855 = 17.3855\n$$\n\nTaking the floor and adding 1:\n\n$$\n\\lfloor 17.3855 \\rfloor + 1 = 17 + 1 = 18\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{18}\n$$",
